.TH ZIP 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zip \- archives ZIP / package and compress files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zip
[-rjq0] archive.zip file...
.br
.B unzip
[-ltpon] [-d dir] archive.zip [member...]
.br
.B zipinfo
archive.zip
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
zip stores files in a ZIP archive (deflate when it shrinks the data). unzip lists (-l), tests (-t), prints (-p) or extracts members; stored and deflated
entries, dynamic and fixed Huffman blocks, CRC-32 checked. Files up to 8 MB; no ZIP64.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -r
Recurse into directories.
.TP
.B -j
Junk the paths.
.TP
.B -0
Store only.
.TP
.B -d dir
Extract into dir.
.TP
.B -o
Overwrite without asking.
.TP
.B -n
Never overwrite.
.SH SEE ALSO
gzip(1), tar(1)
